# 6. EXPENSE MANAGEMENT

Employees should be able to create expenses.

Examples:

```text
Travel
Hotel
Food
Taxi
Fuel
Parking
Internet
Mobile
Office Supplies
Client Meeting
Training
Business Development
Other
```

Do not hard-code categories.

Categories must be configurable by tenant administrators.

---

# 7. EXPENSE MODEL

Create an expense entity using existing database conventions.

Potential fields:

```text
id
tenant_id
employee_id
expense_category_id
expense_date
amount
currency
merchant
description
location
payment_method
receipt_file_id
status
submitted_at
approved_at
rejected_at
created_at
updated_at
created_by
updated_by
```

Use the existing ID strategy.

---

# 8. EXPENSE STATUS

Implement a controlled state machine:

```text
DRAFT
SUBMITTED
UNDER_REVIEW
APPROVED
REJECTED
RETURNED
REIMBURSEMENT_PENDING
REIMBURSED
CANCELLED
```

Invalid status transitions must be rejected.

---

# 9. EXPENSE LIFECYCLE

Expected workflow:

```text
Employee
   ↓
Create Expense
   ↓
Attach Receipt
   ↓
Submit
   ↓
Manager/HR Review
   ↓
Approve
   ↓
Reimbursement Queue
   ↓
Payroll/Finance
   ↓
Reimbursed
```

Rejected:

```text
Submit
 ↓
Reject
 ↓
Employee receives reason
```

Returned:

```text
Review
 ↓
Return for correction
 ↓
Employee edits
 ↓
Resubmit
```

---

# 10. EXPENSE CATEGORY MASTER

Create configurable categories.

Example:

```text
Travel
Accommodation
Meals
Transportation
Fuel
Office Supplies
Communication
Training
Client Entertainment
Medical
Miscellaneous
```

Fields:

```text
id
tenant_id
code
name
description
max_amount
requires_receipt
requires_approval
taxable
status
effective_from
effective_to
```

---

# 11. EXPENSE POLICY ENGINE

Create configurable policies.

Policies may define:

```text
Maximum claim amount
Receipt requirement
Daily limit
Category limit
Employee grade limit
Department limit
Location limit
Currency
Approval requirement
```

Example:

```text
Hotel:
Maximum ₹5,000/day

Meals:
Maximum ₹1,000/day

Taxi:
Maximum ₹2,000/day
```

Do NOT hard-code these limits.

---

# 12. POLICY VIOLATIONS

Detect:

```text
Exceeded category limit
Missing receipt
Duplicate expense
Invalid date
Invalid currency
Exceeded daily limit
Exceeded monthly limit
```

Classify:

```text
WARNING
ERROR
BLOCKING
```

---

# 13. EXPENSE DUPLICATE DETECTION

Detect potential duplicates using combinations such as:

```text
Employee
Date
Amount
Merchant
Category
Receipt
```

Do not automatically reject legitimate expenses merely because they look similar.

Mark them for review where appropriate.

---

# 14. RECEIPT MANAGEMENT

Employees should be able to attach receipts.

Support:

```text
PDF
JPG
JPEG
PNG
WEBP
```

Use existing file storage.

Do NOT store large binary files directly in PostgreSQL unless the existing architecture explicitly requires it.

Prefer:

```text
Object Storage
File Metadata
Secure Download
```

---

# 15. RECEIPT SECURITY

Receipts may contain sensitive information.

Implement:

```text
Authenticated access
Authorization checks
Tenant isolation
Signed/temporary URLs where supported
Access logging
```

Never expose publicly accessible receipt URLs.

---

# 16. FILE VALIDATION

Validate:

```text
File extension
MIME type
File size
File signature
```

Do not trust the filename extension alone.

Reject dangerous file types.

---

# 17. RECEIPT DOWNLOAD

Only authorized users can access receipts.

Employee:

```text
Own expense receipts
```

Manager:

```text
Receipts within authorized approval scope
```

HR/Finance:

```text
Authorized tenant scope
```

Prevent IDOR.

---

# 18. EXPENSE SUBMISSION

Before submission validate:

```text
Category exists
Employee exists
Date valid
Amount valid
Currency valid
Receipt requirement satisfied
Policy satisfied
Tenant matches
```

Never trust frontend validation alone.

---

# 19. EXPENSE DATE RULES

Prevent inappropriate dates according to policy.

Support configuration:

```text
Past-date allowance
Future-date allowance
Claim submission deadline
```

Example:

```text
Expense Date:
01 Sep

Submission:
Within 30 days
```

---

