```

Items:

```text
id
claim_id
category_id
expense_date
amount
merchant
description
receipt_file_id
```

---

# 24. CLAIM TOTAL

The backend must calculate:

```text
Claim Total
=
SUM(Approved Expense Items)
```

Never trust a frontend-provided total.

---

# 25. PARTIAL APPROVAL

Support:

```text
Submitted:
₹20,000

Approved:
₹17,000

Rejected:
₹3,000
```

Each expense item must maintain its own approval result where required.

---

# 26. APPROVAL COMMENTS

Approvers should be able to provide:

```text
Approval comment
Rejection reason
Return reason
```

Comments must be retained in history.

---

# 27. APPROVAL WORKFLOW

Reuse Phase 6 workflow.

Possible flow:

```text
Employee
 ↓
Manager
 ↓
Finance/HR
 ↓
Final Approval
```

The number of approval levels should be configurable.

---

# 28. APPROVAL RULES

Allow workflow conditions based on:

```text
Amount
Department
Employee Grade
Location
Expense Category
Manager
Organization
```

Example:

```text
≤ ₹5,000
Manager approval

₹5,001–₹25,000
Manager + Finance

> ₹25,000
Manager + Finance + HR/Admin
```

Do not hard-code these thresholds.

---

# 29. EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT

Approved expenses enter reimbursement.

Statuses:

```text
PENDING
PROCESSING
PROCESSED
FAILED
REIMBURSED
CANCELLED
```

---

# 30. REIMBURSEMENT METHODS

Prepare support for:

```text
PAYROLL
BANK_TRANSFER
MANUAL
OTHER
```

Actual banking integration is NOT required unless explicitly requested.

---

# 31. PAYROLL INTEGRATION

Integrate reimbursement with Phase 7.

Example:

```text
Salary
+
Approved Reimbursement
-
Deductions
=
Net Payable
```

However, reimbursement should remain separately identifiable from salary.

Do NOT simply merge reimbursement into Basic/Gross salary.

---

# 32. PAYROLL LINE ITEM

Create payroll integration using an explicit line item:

```text
REIMBURSEMENT
```

Example:

```text
Basic Salary       ₹40,000
HRA                ₹16,000
Other Earnings      ₹5,000
---------------------------
Gross               ₹61,000

Expense Reimbursement
                     ₹7,500

Deductions           ₹6,000

Net Payable         ₹62,500
```

The reimbursement amount must remain traceable.

---

# 33. REIMBURSEMENT TAXABILITY

Prepare configuration:

```text
taxable
non_taxable
partially_taxable
```

Do not hard-code tax treatment.

---

# 34. REIMBURSEMENT SNAPSHOT

Once reimbursement enters finalized payroll, preserve:

```text
Expense ID
Claim ID
Approved Amount
Employee
Payroll Period
Policy
Approval History
```

Historical payroll must not change if the expense record is later edited.

---

# 35. EXPENSE REVERSAL

If an already reimbursed expense needs correction:

Do NOT modify historical reimbursement directly.

Use:

```text
Reversal
Adjustment
Recovery
```

and maintain audit history.

---

