# 40. LOAN ELIGIBILITY

Prepare configurable rules:

```text
Minimum employment duration
Maximum loan amount
Salary multiple
Existing loan restriction
Department eligibility
Employee status
```

Example:

```text
Maximum Loan
=
3 × Monthly Basic Salary
```

Do not hard-code the multiplier.

---

# 41. LOAN REPAYMENT

Generate repayment schedules.

Example:

```text
Principal:
₹120,000

Tenure:
12 months

Monthly Principal:
₹10,000
```

If interest applies, calculate according to configured method.

---

# 42. INTEREST TYPES

Prepare support for:

```text
NO_INTEREST
FLAT
REDUCING_BALANCE
```

If reducing-balance calculation is implemented, ensure the formula is tested extensively.

---

# 43. LOAN INSTALLMENT

Each installment should track:

```text
installment_number
due_date
principal
interest
total
paid_amount
remaining_amount
status
```

Statuses:

```text
PENDING
PARTIALLY_PAID
PAID
OVERDUE
WAIVED
CANCELLED
```

---

# 44. LOAN PAYROLL INTEGRATION

Approved loan repayments can become payroll deductions.

Example:

```text
Monthly Salary:
₹70,000

Loan Installment:
₹10,000

Other deductions:
₹5,000

Net:
₹55,000
```

Payroll must identify:

```text
LOAN_REPAYMENT
```

separately.

---

# 45. LOAN BALANCE

Maintain:

```text
Original Principal
Paid Principal
Remaining Principal
Interest
Paid Interest
Remaining Interest
Outstanding Balance
```

Do not derive historical balances only from mutable current configuration.

---

# 46. LOAN PREPAYMENT

Prepare support for:

```text
Full Prepayment
Partial Prepayment
```

Any applicable charges should be configurable.

---

# 47. LOAN PAUSE

Support controlled pause:

```text
Loan
 ↓
Pause
 ↓
Reason
 ↓
Approval
```

Examples:

```text
Unpaid Leave
Special Arrangement
Management Approval
```

Do not automatically pause loans based on assumptions.

---

# 48. SALARY ADVANCE

Implement short-term salary advances.

Example:

```text
Employee requests:
₹20,000

Approved:
₹20,000

Recovery:
₹5,000/month × 4 months
```

