# 52. FINANCIAL LEDGER CONCEPT

Create a traceable transaction history.

Financial events:

```text
Expense Approved
Expense Reimbursed
Loan Disbursed
Loan Repayment
Salary Advance Disbursed
Advance Recovery
Adjustment
Reversal
```

Each event should be traceable.

---

# 53. TRANSACTION MODEL

If appropriate, create:

```text
employee_financial_transactions
```

Potential fields:

```text
id
tenant_id
employee_id
transaction_type
reference_type
reference_id
amount
currency
direction
transaction_date
description
status
created_at
created_by
```

Use the existing financial architecture if one already exists.

---

# 54. TRANSACTION TYPES

Examples:

```text
EXPENSE_REIMBURSEMENT
LOAN_DISBURSEMENT
LOAN_REPAYMENT
SALARY_ADVANCE
SALARY_ADVANCE_RECOVERY
ADJUSTMENT
REVERSAL
```

---

# 55. FINANCIAL TRANSACTION IMMUTABILITY

Financial history must not be silently rewritten.

For finalized transactions use:

```text
Adjustment
Reversal
Correction
```

instead of destructive updates.

---

# 56. DOUBLE-ENTRY PREPARATION

Do not implement a full accounting ledger unless required.

However, design financial events so a future accounting module can consume:

```text
Transaction ID
Employee
Amount
Currency
Transaction Type
Date
Reference
Department
Cost Center
```

---

# 57. COST CENTER

Prepare optional support for:

```text
Cost Center
Project
Client
Department
Branch
```

Expenses may be allocated against them.

---

# 58. EXPENSE PROJECT ALLOCATION

Support:

```text
Expense
 ↓
Project
 ↓
Cost Center
```

Do not require project information if the tenant does not use projects.

---

# 59. CURRENCY

Support multi-currency expenses.

Fields:

```text
expense_currency
base_currency
exchange_rate
base_amount
```

Example:

```text
USD Expense:
$100

Exchange Rate:
₹84

Base Amount:
₹8,400
```

Do not hard-code exchange rates.

---

# 60. EXCHANGE RATE SOURCE

Prepare an interface:

```text
ExchangeRateService
```

Future integrations can provide rates.

Do not make external API calls from the core calculation layer without abstraction.

---

# 61. ROUNDING

Use:

```text
Decimal
```

for all financial calculations.

PostgreSQL:

```text
NUMERIC
```

Do NOT use floating-point arithmetic for money.

---

# 62. EXPENSE LIMIT CALCULATION

Use precise monetary calculations.

Example:

```text
Claim = ₹5,999.75
Limit = ₹6,000
```

This should not incorrectly fail due to floating-point precision.

