# 73. EMPLOYEE ACCESS

Employee can:

```text
Create expense
Edit draft expense
Submit expense
View own expenses
View own reimbursements
Create loan request
View own loan
View repayment schedule
Create salary advance request
View own advance
```

Employee cannot:

```text
Approve own expense
Approve own loan
Modify approved reimbursement
View another employee's financial information
```

---

# 74. MANAGER ACCESS

Managers can see only employees within their authorization scope.

They may:

```text
Review expenses
Approve/reject expenses
Review loan requests
Approve/reject where authorized
```

---

# 75. FINANCE/HR ACCESS

Authorized finance/HR users may:

```text
Manage policies
Process reimbursements
Manage loans
Manage advances
Review financial reports
Process recovery
```

subject to permissions.

---

# 76. TENANT ISOLATION

Critical security tests:

```text
Tenant A
   X
Tenant B
```

Tenant A must never access:

```text
Expenses
Receipts
Loans
Advances
Reimbursements
Financial Transactions
Reports
Policies
```

belonging to Tenant B.

---

# 77. IDOR PROTECTION

Test attempts such as:

```text
GET /api/v1/expenses/{other_employee_expense}
GET /api/v1/loans/{other_employee_loan}
GET /api/v1/payslips/{other_employee_payslip}
GET /api/v1/receipts/{other_receipt}
```

must enforce authorization.

---

# 78. MASS ASSIGNMENT PROTECTION

Never allow clients to directly set:

```text
tenant_id
approved_by
approval_status
reimbursement_status
financial_status
created_by
```

unless authorized and handled server-side.

---

# 79. AUDIT LOGGING

Audit:

```text
Expense Created
Expense Updated
Expense Submitted
Expense Approved
Expense Rejected
Expense Returned
Expense Reimbursed

Loan Created
Loan Approved
Loan Rejected
Loan Disbursed
Loan Paused
Loan Repayment
Loan Closed

Advance Created
Advance Approved
Advance Disbursed
Advance Recovery
Advance Closed
```

---

# 80. AUDIT DETAILS

Store:

```text
Actor
Action
Entity
Entity ID
Timestamp
Previous Status
New Status
Reason
IP/device metadata where supported by existing audit architecture
```

Do not store unnecessary sensitive information.

---

# 81. NOTIFICATIONS

Use the existing notification system.

Events:

```text
Expense Submitted
Expense Approved
Expense Rejected
Expense Returned
Expense Reimbursed

Loan Submitted
Loan Approved
Loan Rejected
Loan Disbursed
Loan Installment Due

Advance Submitted
Advance Approved
Advance Recovered
```

---

# 82. EMAIL NOTIFICATIONS

Where appropriate:

```text
Expense Approved
Expense Rejected
Reimbursement Completed
Loan Approved
Loan Disbursed
Advance Approved
```

Use secure authenticated links.

Do not expose unnecessary financial information in email content.

---

# 83. BACKGROUND JOBS

Use existing Celery infrastructure where available.

Potential jobs:

```text
process_reimbursements
generate_expense_reports
generate_financial_reports
process_loan_repayments
process_advance_recoveries
send_financial_notifications
```

Jobs must be:

```text
Idempotent
Retry-safe
Tenant-aware
Auditable
```

---

# 84. DUPLICATE JOB PROTECTION

A retry must NOT:

```text
Reimburse twice
Recover loan installment twice
Recover advance twice
Create duplicate transaction
```

Use idempotency keys and database constraints.

---

# 85. DATABASE TRANSACTIONS

Financial operations must be transactional.

Example:

```text
BEGIN

Validate approval
Validate amount
Create financial transaction
Create reimbursement record
Update status
Create audit record

COMMIT
```

If any operation fails:

```text
ROLLBACK
```

---

# 86. DATABASE TABLES

Potential tables:

```text
expense_categories
expense_policies
expenses
expense_claims
expense_items
expense_receipts
expense_approvals
reimbursements
loan_types
loan_policies
employee_loans
loan_installments
salary_advances
advance_recoveries
employee_financial_transactions
```

Do not create duplicates if equivalent existing models already exist.

---

# 87. DATABASE CONSTRAINTS

Use:

```text
Foreign Keys
Unique Constraints
Check Constraints
Tenant Constraints
Status Constraints
Effective Date Constraints
```

Examples:

```text
amount > 0
approved_amount >= 0
approved_amount <= submitted_amount
```

where appropriate.

---

# 88. DATABASE INDEXES

Index:

```text
tenant_id
employee_id
status
expense_date
claim_id
loan_id
advance_id
created_at
due_date
```

Composite indexes where useful:

```text
tenant_id + employee_id
tenant_id + status
tenant_id + expense_date
tenant_id + due_date
```

Avoid unnecessary indexes.

---

