# 99. PAYROLL RECONCILIATION

Before payroll finalization verify:

```text
Approved reimbursement
+
Loan repayment
+
Advance recovery
```

matches payroll line items.

Example:

```text
Approved reimbursement:
₹50,000

Payroll reimbursement:
₹50,000

Difference:
₹0
```

If difference exists:

```text
BLOCK PAYROLL FINALIZATION
```

or flag according to configured policy.

---

# 100. PAYROLL SNAPSHOT

When payroll is locked, snapshot:

```text
Reimbursement
Loan Repayment
Advance Recovery
Adjustment
```

Historical payroll must remain unchanged.

---

# 101. EMPLOYEE FINANCIAL SUMMARY

Create an employee-level summary:

```text
Salary
Expenses
Reimbursements
Loans
Loan Outstanding
Advances
Advance Outstanding
Financial Transactions
```

Respect RBAC.

---

# 102. PERFORMANCE

Optimize for:

```text
1,000 employees
5,000 employees
10,000 employees
```

Avoid N+1 queries.

Use:

```text
Prefetch
Select related
Batch queries
Aggregations
Indexes
Background jobs
```

where appropriate.

---

# 103. CONCURRENCY TESTS

Test:

```text
Two users approve same expense
Two users process reimbursement
Two workers process same reimbursement
Two payroll workers recover same installment
Loan installment processed twice
Advance recovery processed twice
```

Only one valid financial transaction should be created.

---

# 104. IDEMPOTENCY

Every financial processing operation should have an idempotency strategy.

Examples:

```text
expense_id + reimbursement_id
loan_id + installment_id
advance_id + recovery_id
```

must not create duplicate financial transactions.

---

# 105. SECURITY TESTS

Test:

```text
Cross-tenant expense access
Cross-tenant receipt access
Cross-tenant loan access
Cross-tenant advance access
Cross-tenant financial report access
Employee accessing another employee
Manager accessing unauthorized department
Unauthorized reimbursement
Unauthorized loan approval
```

---

