# FINAL INSTRUCTION TO THE AI CODING AGENT

**Inspect first. Implement second.**

Do not rewrite working Phase 1–7 modules.

Do not duplicate:

```text
Authentication
RBAC
Tenant
Employee
Approval
Payroll
Salary
Audit
Notification
File Storage
```

systems.

Reuse the existing AxonTimeHR architecture.

Implement Phase 8 incrementally:

```text
1. Repository analysis
2. Architecture design
3. Expense category master
4. Expense policy engine
5. Expense creation
6. Receipt management
7. Expense claims
8. Approval integration
9. Reimbursement
10. Payroll integration
11. Loan types
12. Loan policies
13. Loan requests
14. Loan eligibility
15. Loan approval
16. Loan disbursement
17. Loan repayment schedule
18. Loan payroll deduction
19. Salary advances
20. Advance recovery
21. Financial transaction history
22. Financial dashboards
23. Reports
24. Notifications
25. Background jobs
26. Security
27. Audit
28. Concurrency protection
29. Idempotency
30. Reconciliation
31. Testing
32. Performance optimization
33. Documentation
34. Full regression
```

After every major component:

```text
Implement
   ↓
Run tests
   ↓
Fix failures
   ↓
Validate database
   ↓
Validate financial calculations
   ↓
Validate authorization
   ↓
Validate tenant isolation
   ↓
Validate payroll integration
   ↓
Run regression
   ↓
Continue
```

The final Phase 8 implementation must be:

**production-ready, secure, multi-tenant, financially accurate, auditable, configurable, scalable, payroll-integrated, and extensible.**

Most importantly:

**Never directly rewrite finalized financial transactions. Use immutable transaction records, adjustments, reversals, approvals, and audit trails so AxonTimeHR maintains a trustworthy financial history.**

**Recommended next phase:** after Phase 8, Phase 9 should focus on **advanced HR operations—Performance Management, Goals/KPIs, Appraisals, 360° Feedback, Training/Learning and Employee Engagement**, which will make AxonTimeHR much closer to a complete enterprise HRMS.
